  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Plan Your Data Story\r\n\r\nYour Task: Choose something real that you can count, and plan a program that turns your numbers into a picture. Work only in `story_plan.txt` for now. You will use `main.py` in the next level.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Pick a story: something you can count each day or each round, like minutes you practice, points you score, or songs you play. Choose something you are comfortable sharing.\r\n2. Fill out MY STORY and MY NUMBERS in `story_plan.txt`.\r\n3. Fill out MY HAND TRACE. Make up your first three numbers, then work out the total after each one and the average of the three.\r\n4. Describe MY PICTURE, then write MY AI PROMPT for AI Tutor. Name the variables it should use (`value`, `j`, `average`) and tell it not to calculate the total or the average.\r\n5. Save your plan. You will use it in the next level.\r\n\r\n::: details [Need an idea for your story?]\r\n\r\n- Minutes you practice a skill, a game, or an instrument each day\r\n- Points you score in each game of a season\r\n- Songs, episodes, or videos you watch each day\r\n- Steps, laps, or shots in each practice\r\n- Your own idea: anything you can count with a whole number from 1 to 100\r\n\r\n:::",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
